=== NEW PAGES - ranked by effort vs reward ===

1. Proofreading vs copyediting vs developmental - comparison page
   Highest-volume query in the sector. Informational so it ranks without fighting
   commercial intent. Currently buried in a homepage FAQ accordion, which is the
   worst possible place for it.

2. Pricing page + word count calculator
   "how much does it cost to edit a book" is high volume AND high intent. Open
   pricing is a competitive weapon and it's currently hidden. Small JS calculator:
   enter word count, get all three prices. Earns links, keeps people on page.

3. Book blurb & Amazon description writing
   New revenue line, low delivery effort, indie authors search it constantly.
   Natural upsell after a copyedit.

4. Ebook & print formatting / KDP
   Already offered, distinct search, commercial intent. Currently one accordion item.

5. Memoir & life story
   Underserved. Older, more affluent, emotionally motivated buyers. Pairs with
   developmental editing.

6. Cover letters
   Obvious companion to the CV page. The two cross-link naturally.

7. Crime & thriller editing
   Completes the genre set alongside romance and SFF.

8. Medicine & dentistry personal statements
   Very high intent. UK applicants search this separately from generic UCAS help.


